+/**
+ * Whether a declaration at `scopePrefix` owns the bare spelling of `name`.
+ *
+ * A bare key is not a declaration. It is how a using-directive reaches a namespaced name, so several
+ * declarations compete for the one slot, and C++ hands it to the **nearest** — a file-scope
+ * `static constexpr uint64 Threshold = 5` is `Threshold`, while `namespace Port { enum Limits
+ * { Threshold = 55 }; }` declares `Port::Threshold` and is only reachable bare through a
+ * using-directive. Both tables here used to take the slot unconditionally and delete the other kind's
+ * entry with it, so whichever was collected last won and a qualified read of one changed the value of
+ * the other (F213).
+ *
+ * Nearest wins; equal scope keeps last-writer-wins, which is what lets a contract shadow a qpi.h
+ * constant of the same name. Precedence is by **scope**, never by kind of declaration: an earlier
+ * attempt that made a `constexpr` beat an enum member outright was the same bug mirrored, and turned
+ * 17 corpus rows red.
